Subject: query-string: read the default export of ESM-only decode-uri-component
Origin: DHI-internal (pnpm patchedDependencies entry for the Kibana build)
Base-Tree: tarball https://registry.npmjs.org/query-string/-/query-string-6.13.2.tgz sha256:0c99cd2bfe87a1475f42bc36cac4624c114c7bd3ec969ef1d560fe26b6336edb
Verify: cmd `DHI_TEST_IMAGE=dhi/kibana:9.5.5-debian13 go test ./image/kibana/tests/browser -count=1 -v` expect "--- PASS: TestBrowserRegression"
Forwarded: not-needed (query-string 8.0.0 and later use an ESM default import, which resolves either decode-uri-component build)
Drop-When: dependency query-string >= 8.0.0

The Kibana package pins decode-uri-component to 0.5.1, which ships only as an ES module with a default export. query-string 6.13.2 loads it with require() and calls the result directly, so both webpack and Node hand it the module namespace object and the first decoded URL throws "decodeComponent is not a function", which breaks the Dashboards app. Reading the default export, with a fallback to the module itself, keeps query-string working with the 0.5.x line and with the older CommonJS 0.2.x line.

diff --git a/index.js b/index.js
--- a/index.js
+++ b/index.js
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 'use strict';
 const strictUriEncode = require('strict-uri-encode');
-const decodeComponent = require('decode-uri-component');
+const decodeUriComponentModule = require('decode-uri-component');
+const decodeComponent = decodeUriComponentModule.default || decodeUriComponentModule;
 const splitOnFirst = require('split-on-first');
 
 const isNullOrUndefined = value => value === null || value === undefined;
